.TH P3M-CHURN 1 "@DATE@" "p3m @VERSION@" "p3m Manual"
.SH NAME
p3m-churn \- estimate the change rate of a path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p3m-churn
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.IR PATH ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B p3m-churn
helps decide whether, and how, to add a path to a replication job.
It scans
.I PATH
repeatedly at a fixed interval and compares each scan with the previous one to
find files that were
.BR created ,
.B modified
(size or modification time differ),
changed in
.B metadata
only (change time differs but size and modification time do not) or
.BR deleted .
The first scan is the baseline and reports no changes.
.PP
When the run ends a report is printed on standard output with:
.IP \(bu 2
the change rate per interval (average and peak) and extrapolated per day,
for files and for data;
.IP \(bu 2
the data a replication job would have to re-send, taken as the size of the
created and modified files (whole-file replication; block or delta based tools
move less);
.IP \(bu 2
the
.B hot files
that changed in the most scans, and the
.B hot directories
(changes rolled up to a chosen depth, which also exposes create/delete churn
from temporary files whose names never repeat);
.IP \(bu 2
notes on what the figures imply for replication: how concentrated the change
is, which files are rewritten continuously, and whether the window is long
enough to trust the daily figures.
.PP
A scan that fails to read a directory does not count that directory's files as
deleted.
Symbolic links are never followed.
Changes between two scans are collapsed: a file rewritten several times within
one interval counts once, so the reported rates are lower bounds.
Shorten the interval to resolve bursts.
.PP
State carried between scans is 40 bytes per file in hash tables, roughly 60 to
115 bytes per file, plus the path of every file that has changed (see
.BR \-\-max\-tracked ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " \fISECONDS\fR"
Time between the starts of consecutive scans (default 300, minimum 0.1).
A scan that overruns the interval is followed immediately by the next.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-count " \fIN\fR"
Stop after
.I N
scans in total, including the baseline (at least 2).
By default the tool runs until stopped.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-duration " \fISECONDS\fR"
Start no new scan after this many seconds.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-top " \fIN\fR"
Length of the hot-file and hot-directory lists (default 20).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-group\-depth " \fIN\fR"
Roll directory changes up to
.I N
levels below each
.I PATH
(default 2).
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " PATTERN"
Skip entries whose name or full path matches the glob
.IR PATTERN .
May be repeated.
Excluded directories are not entered.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-tracked " N"
Remember at most
.I N
distinct changed file paths (default 1000000).
Changes to further files are still counted in the totals and the directory
roll-up, but are not listed per file.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
Scan threads (default: the number of online CPUs).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write one CSV row per scan:
.IR scan ,
.IR start ,
.IR duration_s ,
.IR files ,
.IR bytes ,
.IR dirs ,
.IR created ,
.IR modified ,
.IR metadata ,
.IR deleted ,
.IR bytes_changed ,
.IR bytes_deleted ,
.IR errors .
.TP
.BI \-\-hot\-csv " FILE"
Write every tracked changed file to
.IR FILE ,
most active first:
.IR path ,
.IR events ,
.IR pct_scans ,
.IR created ,
.IR modified ,
.IR bytes_changed ,
.IR last_size ,
.IR last_scan .
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Do not print a line per scan on standard error.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
The first
.B SIGINT
or
.B SIGTERM
lets the scan in progress finish and then prints the report, so
.B Ctrl\-C
is the normal way to end an open-ended run.
A second signal aborts the scan in progress (its totals are discarded; changes
it had already recorded against individual files and directories remain in the
hot lists).
A third quits at once without a report.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A report was produced and no scan errors occurred.
.TP
.B 1
Fewer than two scans completed, or scan errors occurred (the report is still
printed).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sample a share every 5 minutes for a day, saving the data:
.PP
.RS
.nf
p3m\-churn \-i 300 \-t 86400 \-o scans.csv \-\-hot\-csv hot.csv /srv/share
.fi
.RE
.PP
A quick look: six scans a minute apart, ignoring scratch files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
p3m\-churn \-i 60 \-c 6 \-\-exclude '*.tmp' \-\-exclude '.cache' /data
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p3m (7),
.BR p3m\-sync (1),
.BR p3m\-stats (1),
.BR p3m\-ls (1)
